  "evidence": [
    "Source palette.h HSV is three doubles h/s/v. RGB_to_HSV writes this type, get_nearest_palette_index consumes it in 24-byte records, and current game tint callers use it directly.",
    "Pinned create_table 0x005FED40-0x005FEE78 copies three-double records and passes them to RGB_to_HSV 0x00628DB0 and get_nearest_palette_index 0x005FF630. Current local HSVLocal duplicates HSV then accesses it through unrelated typed pointers.",
    "Replace duplicate local record type with existing HSV, retaining stack array extent, loop bounds, signed parameters, and separate brightness multiplies. No public header/ABI, bounds checks or bug fixes. Scope includes complete palette TU measurements for collateral.",
    "Require native baseline/candidate comparison, actual-body host controls, source claims/references and fresh build/link before coordinator integration. Preserve historical claims on temporary regression; no full-game acceptance inferred."
  ],
  "intent": "Use the actual shared HSV type for Palette brightness-table stack records; preserve arithmetic order, unchecked ranges and historical exactness obligations.",
